# Sales Report Rules

**Every uploaded or replaced sales CSV must follow these rules** — bundled seed (`data/reports/Sales-Report.csv`), Data Analyst upload, and API `POST /api/reports`.

## Net Sales / store totals = full CSV Total

**All users** see Net Sales and store sales that match the CSV **Total** column sum for the filtered window — including repairs, SPO, battery, `ITEM` memos, `JVV-*` tickets, pads, winders, and other line types present in the file.

Do **not** strip rows from Net Sales / store / department / design / salesperson / overall revenue totals to “clean” the report. Parse keeps blank departments; dashboard queries use raw parsed rows.

## Soft-hidden from Top Vendor Models only

These still count in Net Sales / store / vendor / department / salesperson totals, but must **not** appear in Top Vendor Models / top-product lists (except **Rozina** — see below):

| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| Item # / SKU `ITEM` | Repair / SPO / custom-order / finance memos — revenue in Net Sales; hide from Top Vendor Models only |
| Item # / SKU starts with `JVV-` | Store repair/service tickets — revenue in Net Sales; hide from Top Vendor Models only (no margin %) |
| Vendor model `WG2787` | Hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |
| Vendor model `WG670` | Threaded earring post — findings; hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |
| Vendor model `2200-2218` | Screwback earring back / pad — findings; hidden from top vendor models (still in net sales) |

**Rozina exception:** username `rozina` sees **all sold lines** in Top Vendor Models (incl. `ITEM` / `JVV-*`), grouped with Total/net, via `showsAllSoldInTopVendorModels()` + `includeHiddenTopModels`. Margin on repair/memo lines shows as red `—`. Everyone else keeps soft-hide on Top Models only. **ITEM display:** vendor-model column shows only `ITEM`; description stays in the product/description column (no `ITEM · {desc}` duplication). Grouping key internally remains `ITEM · {description}`.

### Top Vendor Models — cancelled SKU legs (ranking only)

Cross-txn / exchange returns stay in **Net Sales**. For **Top Vendor Models / model detail / SKU expand only** (non-Rozina), `collapseCancelledSkuLegs()` drops matching sale↔return legs (**any day in the filter window**, prefers nearest prior sale): (1) same store + SKU + abs net, (2) same store + abs net (size / Y-suffix exchange), (3) same SKU + abs net (cross-store cancel). Also hide models with units &gt; 0 and |net| &lt; $1. Does **not** change store Net Sales totals. Rozina skips cancel-collapse so her Top Models match CSV lines.

### Implementation

- **Net Sales path:** raw parsed rows (`query-sales` / `loadRankRows` / refresh snapshot) — no `filterExcludedSalesRows()`
- **Top Models soft-hide:** `isHiddenFromTopVendorModelsRow()` / `filterTopProductSkus()` / `groupRows` in `src/lib/utils.ts` + `sales-aggregate.ts`
- **Top Models cancel:** `collapseCancelledSkuLegs()` + `signedWholesaleUnitCost()` in `src/lib/sales/top-models-wholesale-margin.ts` (`TOP_MODELS_MARGIN_RULES_VERSION`)
- Legacy helpers `isExcludedSalesRow` / `filterExcludedSalesRows` remain for optional tooling but must **not** gate dashboard Net Sales
- Cached sales versions rebuild when `SALES_EXCLUSION_RULES_VERSION` or `TOP_MODELS_MARGIN_RULES_VERSION` bumps

When changing Top Models soft-hide rules, update `src/lib/utils.ts` and this file.

## Profit / margin

- Prefer **Whole Cost rules** (`wholeCostFromRules` / `calculatorWholesaleUnitCost`) when a rule matches — GOLD JEWL+UV ÷1.3, Diamond+UV ÷8.8, watches, fixed SKUs, etc.
- **Sales dashboard / daily report base = Sales Amount** (gross), not Tag Price. Price calculator stays on Tag.
- Row margin = `netRevenue − signedWholesaleUnitCost` (sale subtracts cost; return adds cost back).
- Else when the CSV includes **Profit Amount** and no calculator cost, use that column as row `margin`.
- Last resort if neither applies: `margin = 0` (never use Kash inventory cost alone on sales lines).
- **Real negative %** is allowed when Net &lt; wholesale unit cost — do not hide those.
- **ITEM / JVV repair lines:** no margin % in Top Models (red `—`).

## Bundled default report

- File: `data/reports/Sales-Report.csv`
- Seeded via `src/lib/reports/store.ts`; app refreshes `.data/reports/` when the file changes
- Current seed window: **2025-01-01 → 2026-09-04**
- Companion paycode overlay: `data/reports/Payment-Transactions.csv` (Applied Amt by Transaction # / Pay Code; daily files append / replace same day)

## Paycode overlay (Sales Dashboard only)

Match payment `Transaction #` → sales `Transaction #`. Amounts use **Applied Amt** (not Payment Amt, not line Total). Overlay txn map skips blank Type and Returns/Refunds. Paycodes card, paycode filter, and tap-for-details use payment `Transaction Date` SUMIFS (includes Returns/CR/OL) so each method total matches the payment CSV.

Display and filter by the **method after the store hyphen** (`VJS-CASH` → `CASH`). Never list store prefixes (`VJF`, `VIS`, `VJPB`, `VJS`, …) as paycodes. **HR Management Sales has no paycode filter.**

| Canonical | Aliases (POS truncations) |
|---|---|
| **ACIMA** | ACIMA, ACIM |
| **AFFIRM** | AFFIRM, AFFR, AFRIM |
| **IDDEAL** | IDDEAL, IDEA, IDEAL |
| **PROG** | PROG, PROGR, PROGRE, PROGRESSIVE |
| **SYNC** | SYNC, SYCHY, SYNCH, SYNCHRONY, SYNCHRO, SYNCHY, SYNCY, SYNY, GE |
| **CHK** | CHK, CHECK |
| **WELLS** | WELLS, WELL, WELLS FARGO, WELS, WE |

| POS Pay Code | Dashboard / filter |
|---|---|
| `VJS-CASH`, `VJE-CASH`, bare `CASH` | **CASH** |
| `DBCST-ACIM`, `VJSO-ACIMA` | **ACIMA** |
| `DES-AFFIRM`, `DBCST-AFFR`, `VJST-AFRIM` | **AFFIRM** |
| `VJE-IDDEAL`, `DBCST-IDEA`, `VJSL-IDEAL` | **IDDEAL** |
| `BB-SYNC`, `VJRE-SYNY`, Synchrony truncations | **SYNC** |
| `VJB-PROG`, `VJF-PROGRE`, `HD-PROGR`, `VJLV-PROGRESSIVE` | **PROG** |
| `VJO-WELLS`, `VJPB-WELL`, `DBCST-WELS`, `VJST-WELLS FARGO` | **WELLS** |

Same canonical rule on overlay parse — Cursor daily payment appends stay raw in `Payment-Transactions.csv` and fold in automatically.

| Surface | Amount |
|---|---|
| Unfiltered **Net Sales** | CSV **Total** (unchanged) |
| Paycode ranking / Paycodes card | SUM Applied Amt by **canonical method** for payment legs whose **Transaction Date** is in the dashboard window (POS Excel SUMIFS). Includes CR/OL/CL and Returns/Refunds. Not limited to sales-line tickets. Blank Type / POS total rows stay excluded. Store filter uses the payment `Store` column. Department / design / vendor / class / salesperson filters restrict to those sales tickets. |
| Paycode filter selected (e.g. ACIMA) | Include every alias in that group; Net Sales = that group’s **Applied Amt** for payment legs in the date/store window (same as the Paycodes card). Match payment `Transaction #` to sales lines and allocate by `|Total|` weight. Payment-only CR/OL/return legs still count so the total matches the payment CSV. |

Paycode filter is on **Sales Dashboard** only (store / department / design / class / subclass / salesperson still apply on HR Sales). Implementation: `src/lib/sales/paycode-normalize.ts` + `src/lib/sales/paycode-overlay.ts` (`PAYCODE_OVERLAY_VERSION`).

## Daily append (Cursor)

Umair appends through Cursor, not Data Analyst. Always both files together:

```
npx tsx scripts/append-daily-sales-and-payments.ts <sales.csv> <payments.csv>
```

| File | Lands in | Rules |
|---|---|---|
| Daily sales CSV | `data/reports/Sales-Report.csv` | `normalizeDailySalesCsv()`; same **Transaction Date** replaces that day; Net Sales = CSV **Total** |
| Daily payment CSV | `data/reports/Payment-Transactions.csv` | Keep raw POS Pay Codes; same-day replace; leftover rows upsert by txn + **canonical** pay method + Applied Amt |

After write, the script refreshes sales data, clears the overlay cache, and **fails** if ACIM / AFFR / AFRIM / WELL / WELS / WELLS FARGO / IDEA / … appear as separate overlay labels. Dashboard filter uses the alias groups above (ACIMA = ACIMA+ACIM Applied Amt, etc.).

## Daily append format (always)

Daily sales files use the Umair / POS export shape. Cursor append uses this format (`scripts/append-daily-sales-and-payments.ts`).

| Column in CSV | App field |
|---|---|
| `Item #` | **SKU** (`sku` / `itemNumber`) — same as `SKU #` when present |
| `VendorModel1` | **Vendor model** |
| `Image Dir.` | Product image path — **always store/resolve as `.webp`** (replace `.jpg` / `.jpeg` / `.png` / `.gif`) |
| `Profit Amount` | Row margin (see Profit / margin above) |
| `Transaction Date` | Day key for append/replace-same-day merge |

### Empty spacer columns

Daily files often have blank header cells between fields (double commas). Always run `normalizeDailySalesCsv()` before parse/merge/save — collapse columns whose header is empty; do not invent names for blank headers.

### Zero Total rows

Drop **product** rows where **Total** is `0`. **Keep** `$0` Total **Item # = ITEM** rows (and Description APP / FIN / FINANCE memos) in the seed CSV so Discounting can join the same Transaction # package (approver + financing).

### Discounting — Payment Amt ceiling

When a companion paycode CSV has `Payment Amt`, compare the full transaction package calculation (all product calculator minimums + Mulberry Total) to that payment amount — **not** to the sales-line Total:

- Cash only: calculated = package minimum
- CC only: calculated = package minimum (same as cash — no 3.5% surcharge)
- Cash + CC (no financing): calculated = package minimum; ceiling = cash Payment Amt + CC Payment Amt
- Financing only: calculated = package minimum × financing-term multiplier
- Cash/CC + financing: subtract cash and CC Payment Amt from package minimum, then apply the financing term to the remainder; ceiling = financing Payment Amt only
- Flag only when **calculated > matching Payment Amt**; overage = calculated − Payment Amt
- Any transaction containing a Qty `-1` / negative return leg is excluded entirely
- Keep only the newest sales month in Discounting; paycode uploads prune older-month paycode files

### Implementation

- `src/lib/reports/normalize-daily-sales-csv.ts` — collapse empty columns + Image Dir → webp
- `src/lib/reports/product-image.ts` — `normalizeSalesImageDir()` / `preferWebpFilename()`
- `src/lib/reports/vendor-pos.ts` — maps `Item #` → SKU, `VendorModel1` → vendor model (also accepts historical `SKU #` / `Vendor Model`; prefers non-empty); normalizes `imageDir` at parse
- `src/lib/reports/merge-sales-csv.ts` — append by Transaction Date (same day replaces); copies `Item #` → `SKU #` and `VendorModel1` → `Vendor Model` when merging into the live seed
- `src/lib/reports/merge-payment-csv.ts` + `scripts/append-daily-sales-and-payments.ts` — Cursor daily sales + payment append; alias groups at overlay parse
- Apply normalize on every sales upload path (`api/reports`, `summarizeCsvText`)
- Self-check: `npx tsx scripts/check-daily-sales-csv.ts`

